==English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|universally}}; equivalent to {{suffix|en|universal|ly}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en-us-universally.ogg|Audio (US)|lang=en}}

===Adverb===
{{en-adv}}

# In a [[universal]] manner.
#* {{quote-book|en|title=[[:s:Sikhim and Bhutan|Sikhim and Bhutan]]|author=John Claude White|year=1909|page=12
|passage=My experience of the people was that they were '''universally''' polite, civil, and clean, and during the whole time I spent in the country, I only saw one drunken man.}}
#* {{quote-book|lang=en|year=2006|author=[[w:Edwin Black|Edwin Black]]
|title=Internal Combustion
|chapter=1|url=http://openlibrary.org/works/OL4103950W
|passage=If successful, Edison and Ford&mdash;in 1914&mdash;would move society away from the ever more expensive and then '''universally''' known killing hazards of gasoline cars:&nbsp;[&hellip;]&thinsp;.}}

